mantle rm252
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_maren_tarhand
title the unbroken seal
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=official
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk reads_a_line_of_masts_before_checking_a_letter_seal
likes spiced_cider dice festival_bells misty_dawns
dislikes wet_floors waiting
fears a_smeared_direction a_seal_come_loose
hopes a_letter_safely_delivered an_impression_worth_keeping
topics lore +0.4 land +0.4 pastimes +0.3 travel +0.3 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=steady gossip=guarded refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# reads a row of masts as readily as printed letters, smooths a battered envelope against a sleeve and guards the blank side from idle fingers.

words
oath! = Salt in the ink | Crack my best type
saying! = Read the space between the strokes | An address is enough for a carrier
packet = the folded letter | my sealed packet
sealwax = the hard wax | a dark lump of sealing wax
skytype = the strokes of the masts | the slant of the spars
spice = a curl of spice | the brown cider spice
dicepip = the deep-cut pip | a black dimple in the bone
mark = the straight impression | a firm clean mark
margin = a finger of bare paper | a narrow white margin
paving = a greasy flagstone | a treacherous square of paving
ring = a low bronze note | the roundest bell note
inkpad = the inked pad | a dark pad of ink
bow = a high turned prow | a bow with a slight lift

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : Food across a chapel sill leaves a longer impression than a handsome inscription.
opinion @2 dole for 2 : The share can be small enough to carry in one bowl and still be the difference between working tomorrow and shaking.
opinion @3 houses against 2 : An address belonging to a House is always easy to read. Finding somebody to answer it is a different commission.
opinion @4 merchants against 2 : Somebody prints handsome labels for goods I'd have to sell my boots to buy.
opinion @5 city for 1 : On a clear morning I could read my own city upside down in the Sound.
opinion @6 sump for 2 : The Sump teaches a reader two alphabets, the one on paper and the one that sails.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : A civil welcome. My eyes can come off the paper while you speak. | Come within ordinary speaking distance.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Dawn's made a fine impression. Welcome. | Good morning. There's just enough light for faces now.
line @3 greet [here.weather=fog] : Come through the grey a little. There. | Well met in rather faint light.
line @4 greet.return : I hear you clearly enough. Welcome in turn. | That was a decent address.
line @5 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar shape against the light. Welcome. | Good, no introduction wanted for you.
line @6 farewell : Go with the address clear in your head. | Keep something clean and dry in your pocket.
line @7 farewell.return : Your leave's taken in good order. | I'll let you get along at your own pace.
line @8 again.open : A second impression of a familiar face. | Back across my field of view already.
line @9 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's no seal between family. | Settle here. We know the address well enough.
line @10 hail [pair.band=friends] : Your outline gives you away! | Over here, well within sight!
line @11 react.news : Give the account time to settle. | Speak plainly. I'd have the proper sense of it.
line @12 react.news.known : That account has already gone by me in clear light. | I've retained the impression from the first telling.
line @13 react.news.new : First inkling I've had of that matter. | That throws a shape on a blank space.
line @14 react.news.doubt : I see a break between what happened and what's being said. | That print looks a little too black around the edges.
line @15 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Such news wants a decent quiet round it. | I'd fold that gently before I took it any further.
line @16 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : Set that in fine bold letters. | I'd welcome a bell to carry such a word.
line @17 answer.how : Slow enough to keep a steady impression. | Keeping a clean margin where I can.
line @18 accept_decline : That's a legible answer. | No reason to ask for another impression.
line @19 decline : My word's too much like sealing wax to spend on that. | I'd be putting my mark to something beyond me.
line @20 sympathise : Leave a little room round the hurt. I can wait. | I'll hold a quiet corner for you awhile.
line @21 thank : I'll retain the impression of that kindness. | You've seen something safely into my keeping.
line @22 deflect_thanks : I had the steadier paw for the moment. | A small courtesy needs no inscription.
line @23 preclose : There's a small commission still in my pocket. | Daylight has another use for me yet.
line @24 accept_preclose : I won't put my mark across your errands. | May the right door open easily.
line @25 farewell [here.time=night] : Safe keeping till there's light to read by. | The lamps will pick your road out now.

scene spars
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A ship shows part of its name before the hull comes into view. | I read #skytype# before I look for the painted name.
b : What's in sight by then? | Do the spars spell something?
a : One canted mast can be as plain as the first letter of a word. | Spacing's the trick. Two uprights and a gap can name a ship for me.

scene sealed
when topic=smalltalk
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A sealed letter tells its carrier quite enough on the outside. | The blank side of #packet# is the best side to show a curious wolf.
b : Even if you go on carrying it for weeks? | Couldn't you share who it's meant for?
a : Time wears paper. Gives me no greater claim to what's inside. | Could. I'd gain a minute's talk and lose the quiet of my errand.

scene cidersip
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I leave #spice# in the bottom of my cider till the last sip. | Warm cider shows you where the spice has floated if you wait a moment.
b : Does it get very strong? | I've usually drunk half by then.
a : Strong enough for a cold walk without a second cup. | Tip it toward the light next time. Fine brown letters, all of them.

scene bonedie
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Feel #dicepip# before rolling. Mine's worn quite flat at the centre. | A chipped die writes a crooked record of a game.
b : Can you tell the number by touch? | Would you throw it away?
a : From one to six without looking up from a harbour view. | Mark it for practice. I wouldn't put another wolf's stake on it.

scene firstbells
when topic=season self.likes=festival_bells
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Listen for #ring# under the high festival peal. | I can follow one deep bell clear through a whole bright jumble.
b : What if two of them strike together? | Is it always the loudest?
a : Wait through the next breath. The lower one hangs in the air. | Usually the last to leave. Loud's a poorer way to find it.

scene mistline
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like my morning harbour half erased. | A little mist takes the names off the sterns.
b : How can you name the vessels then? | Isn't that a loss for somebody who knows the fleet?
a : #bow# briefly visible through a thinning patch will do. | A fair examination. The masts still stand plain above the page.

scene slicken
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Step on #paving# and the letter in my pocket will be dipping its corner. | If I lose my feet on wet boards, my paper errand goes into the wash.
b : Tuck it inside your sleeve. | The hem of your coat looks safer.
a : Where sweat can lift the wax? I'll take the longer dry turn. | Higher still, if you please. I've been down on one knee in a puddle.

scene dooragain
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Next time a certain grand door opens, I'd like to have #packet# ready. | My idea of satisfaction is walking home with an empty letter pocket.
b : After all that waiting, what will you say? | You won't miss the weight?
a : Just the direction, spoken out. No speech of mine goes under this seal. | Oddly enough I might. I'll bear the loss.

scene cleanpressure
when topic=work self.job=official self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# you can't repair a bad impression by glaring at it. | A light pull gives you a ghost instead of #mark# at #self.workplace#.
b : What's a better remedy? | Does doubling the ink help?
a : Begin with level type. A crooked letter keeps its own counsel under pressure. | Then you get a fat ghost. Bring up the pressure evenly.

scene frienddawn
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd invite #self.friend# to guess the first mast through the mist. | I ought to take #self.friend# along on a morning I can spare.
b : Would you give a hint? | Have you a particular errand in mind?
a : One. Whether to look for a short slant or a tall upright. | Pleasure only. See how many bows come out of the white water.

scene crowdwait
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : Waiting outside a shut door gives me a fierce interest in the grain of the wood. | I can stand still for a vessel willingly. A closed door's another business.
b : Nothing to read but knots? | The time runs as slowly for both.
a : And whether the latch is wearing bright on either side. | The ship's doing something to reach me. The door can take all season off.

scene enough
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A label ought to show how many hours a thing costs. | Dear cider would taste just as good without the fancy mark on the jug.
b : Whose hours do you put down? | Wouldn't you miss the work on it?
a : Mine, privately. It keeps the wanting inside its proper margin. | I'd admire it on somebody else's table with an easier heart.

scene waterfront
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : By the Sump waterfront a low tide leaves a dark rule under the stones. | Ridgemere's a page you can turn with a change of tide.
b : How far up does the writing go? | What's on the back?
a : Only to where the last wash of water stops. That's an honest boundary. | The underside of the steps. Usually a less flattering account.

scene carryseal
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : Running a thumb over #sealwax# doesn't entitle a wolf to read the letter. | I'd rather lose a throw of dice than win a glimpse beneath a seal.
b : You'd turn down a fine piece of talk. | Even if somebody offered the next stake?
a : That's a small loss against a carrier's word. | Let the busy paws play on without me.

scene whitemargin
when topic=pastimes
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : How would you keep room on a page for a second thought? | Where do you set your hand if there's fresh ink everywhere?
b : Keep the last space empty on purpose. | Lay a strip of clean rag across the dry edge.
a : Yes. #margin# makes even the first thought easier to read. | Better a small clean edge than a whole page of pawmarks.

scene poorwinter
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I can use the back of a notice twice. A loaf doesn't have a second side to eat. | Even the basket looks thinner after a week of paying these prices.
b : You'd give folk something filling if you could. | Would you print the price for everyone to see?
a : I'd put a warm ladle in front of a fine printed promise. | Beside the size of the loaf. That comparison does some work.

scene guessedship
when topic=lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Ask a carrier to name a craft and see which way the eyes go. | Some hulls have a cocked prow as distinct as a bent letter.
b : Toward the stern for the name? | You'd know one even at dusk?
a : That's one way. Up at the spar tells me sooner. | Best of all against the last narrow streak of sky.

scene crumple
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll stand upwind until I get this corner tucked away. | A sheet whistles before it tears in weather like this.
b : Want another paw to hold the fold? | What if the seal lets go?
a : Just shelter the air with your shoulder. The fold stays in my keeping. | Under the coat with it. I'll take a soaking before the letter does.

story ship_in_type [topic=lore]
  : I had a scrap with an inky edge. A little mast-shaped streak and a dash, all it took to make me see a ship turning.
  : I drew a second mast where I thought it belonged and took the scrap to the shore.
  b : Did the drawing match the vessel?
  : From the wall, exactly. From the water stairs my second mast vanished behind the first. Even a good likeness needs an address.

story cider_spill [topic=food]
  : I tipped cider over an old throwaway bill. There was a smell of spice and the ink came up against the bottom of the cup.
  : A whole printed word went on travelling under my drink.
  b : Were you able to read it?
  : In a bright window. Back to front it said fresh. I thought that was a respectable opinion for a cup to hold.

story dry_seal [topic=smalltalk]
  : A rain spot landed square in the middle of some wax on my sleeve. The water stood up like a little glass bead.
  : I kept walking under the eaves, very level, to see which would last longer.
  b : The wax or the water?
  : My patience went first. One good shake, and I put the seal somewhere sensible.

rule @mast
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One glance above the roofs will do. | I'd know that rake against any kind of sky.

rule @page
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=official
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the ink a breath before touching. | Straight from the first pressure.

rule @packet
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wax under wool in this weather. | Dry pocket, steady elbow.

rule @roll
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A fair bone makes a plain account. | Settle the die on the level.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : You appear to have something to bring before me. Go on.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. That outline's legible in any company.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : We've still light enough to make out what matters.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Your business can be stated with your paws quite still.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=official self.workplace] : I help put a clean impression on paper at #self.workplace#.
dlg @6 resident.job : I like a piece of work with a distinct mark left when it's done.
dlg @7 resident.news [world.news] : This has come into view. #world.news#
dlg @8 resident.bye : May your errand find its proper door.

graft resident.hub
choice What's worn the paper so thin? -> sealed_folds
node sealed_folds
say Repeated visits to a grand door. Paper's not generally made to outwait a House. The directions are plain and the seal is still mine to see safe.
choice Would you have another wolf take it? -> sealed_handoff
choice I'll leave your errand alone. -> hub
node sealed_handoff
say Into the intended paw. For something worth carrying away from this conversation, look up at the masts. That's a free page.
choice I'll keep an eye on them. -> hub
choice Good luck with the door. -> bye
